<title>MEXICO: Mexico Q1 current account deficit narrows - govt.</title>
<headline>Mexico Q1 current account deficit narrows - govt.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's current account deficit in the first quarter of 1997 was $406 million, narrowing from the fourth quarter of 1996, Banco de Mexico said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The bank said the current account deficit in the fourth quarter of 1996 was $1.527 billion.</p>
<p>In the first quarter of 1996 the nation posted a current account surplus of $46 million.  </p>
<p>The following table details the current account balance of payments. All figures are in billions of dollars:</p>
<p>					Q1 1997    Q1 1996</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Overall balance		-406	     46</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>	Trade Balance	     1.513	  1.934</p>
<p>	  Exports		  25.042	 21.870</p>
<p>	  Imports		 -23.529	-19.936</p>
<p>	Non-factor Svcs	   0.405	  0.579</p>
<p>	Factor Services	  -3.358	 -3.469</p>
<p>	Transfers		   1.034	  1.002</p>
<p>((--Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9559))</p>
